KZ2 patch 2126: the pipeline template finder scans adjacent regions as one run, so a program
that crosses a region edge is found.

Patch 2071's scout (ld_pt_scan_pass) called rsx_pt_scan once per VirtualQuery region, so ld_pt_hit was told only the
bytes up to the end of that region (`remaining`): a program whose first 16 bytes lie in one region and whose rest
lies in the next adjacent committed region failed the hit's size check (VP: remaining < size; FP: the size scan stops
at the region end) and was never found. jsp found the same class of loss at the end of their finder's chunks (their
`off + 16 <= scan_len` skipped programs starting in a chunk's last 12 bytes; KZ2's step is 16 over page-aligned
regions, so its probes reach the last 16-byte slot, and an earlier change measured every found program at 0 mod 16).
1. rsx_pso_template.h: rsx_pt_run / rsx_pt_run_add: extend the pending run with a region that starts where it ends,
   else scan the pending run (remaining = bytes to the end of the run) and start a new one; len 0 (a gap) flushes.
   rsx_pt_scan_regions: the scout's pass loop, moved here from ld_pt_scan_pass so the host test runs it: readable
   regions go through rsx_pt_run_add, any other region ends the run, the pass ends with a flush (not after a stop).
   Bytes counted as before. RSX_PT_RUN_SPLIT (test only) restores the per-region scan for the negative control.
2. rsx_live_draw.c: ld_pt_query (VirtualQuery: committed, readable, not a guard page) and ld_pt_scan_pass calling
   rsx_pt_scan_regions over the guest reservation [base + 64 KB, base + 3.5 GB).
Not measured in the game yet (needs a cold run; how many programs cross a region edge in KZ2 is unknown, maybe 0:
the guest reservation is one allocation, so adjacent committed pages with the same protection already form one region).
Host test: tools/runtime/test_pt_runs.sh (programs at region ends, across an edge, across a gap, at the end of
memory, through rsx_pt_scan_regions; negative control -DRSX_PT_RUN_SPLIT, the per-region scan, misses the crossing
one and only it, rc and output text checked).

